      "reasoning": "I'm blocking the Spark Reaper with my Caryatid. That's a safe block (2/5 vs 2/3). The Bone Picker is flying over for 3 damage.\n\
\n\
I have `Crushing Canopy` in hand. This is an instant speed effect that can \"Destroy target creature with flying.\" The Bone Picker is a 3/2 Flyer with Deathtouch. It's attacking me.\n\
\n\
I should definitely cast `Crushing Canopy` on the `Bone Picker` right now.\n\
1. It kills a threat.\n\
2. It saves me 3 life.\n\
3. It's mana efficient use of my turn (leaving my main phase mana open was good, but now I use it).\n\
\n\
Let's check mana. I have 4 lands untapped (3 Forests, 1 Plains). Crushing Canopy costs {2}{G}. I can cast it.\n\
\n\
One note: if I cast it now (during Declare Blockers step), it's removed from combat and deals no damage.\n\
Is there any reason to wait? No. If I wait until post-combat, I take 3 damage. Flying threats are annoying.\n\
\n\
So, the plan: Cast Crushing Canopy targeting Bone Picker.\n\
\n\
Wait, let's double check the targetability. Bone Picker doesn't have hexproof.\n\
My hand has: Crushing Canopy, Feat of Resistance, Gargoyle Sentinel, Grave Bramble, Rambunctious Mutt, Secure the Scene, Trusty Retriever.\n\
Mana is fine.\n\
\n\
I will cast Crushing Canopy on Bone Picker.\n\
\n\
Wait, technically I am in the `declare_blockers` step, players get priority. I can cast instants now.\n\
If I cast it now, the creature is destroyed and deals no combat damage.\n\
\n\
Let's execute.\n\
\n\
call `choose_action(choice=\"p28\")` (Crushing Canopy ID).\n\
Then I'll likely have to choose a mode (Destroy creature with flying) and a target (Bone Picker p11).\n\
\n\
The system asks for `choice`.\n\
\n\
Actually, `pass_priority` output showed `Choices (3): Crushing Canopy [id=p28, cast, {2}{G}]...`.\n\
So I select p28.\n\
\n\
One thing: `Feat of Resistance` is also an option, but since I'm not blocking the flyer (can't), giving protection doesn't help block. Giving protection to Caryatid doesn't matter much (it's 2/5 blocking a 2/3, it wins that fight or bounces if 2/3 grows, but 2/3 isn't lethal). Getting rid of the flyer is much better.\n\
\n\
Target: `Bone Picker` is `p11`.\n\
\n\
Let's act.\n\
\n\
After I select the card, the game will ask for mode/targets.\n\
\n\
One detail: `Feat of Resistance` could put a counter on my guy, but killing the 3/2 flyer is way higher value.\n\
\n\
Reaction: Maybe a chat line? I already chatted about blocking the reaper. \"Ew, that bird is so gross too. Be gone!\"\n\
\n\
I'll cast the spell.\n\
\n\
