      "reasoning": "The opponent's turn 7 was eventful. They swung with `Bone Picker` and `Spark Reaper`. My `Caryatid` blocked the Reaper. I used `Crushing Canopy` to kill the Picker before damage. In their second main, they flashed in `Liliana's Standard Bearer` (drawing for the dead Picker) and played `Pit Keeper` (getting something back from grave, likely the Picker again or Stitcher).\n\
\n\
Now it's my turn 8. I drew `Assault Formation`.\n\
\n\
Board state:\n\
Me: 15 life.\n\
Lands: 3 Forest, 1 Plains (4 total).\n\
Creatures: `Carven Caryatid` (2/5), `Selfless Savior` (1/1).\n\
Artifacts: `Warmonger's Chariot` (+2/+2, lets defenders attack).\n\
Hand: `Assault Formation`, `Feat of Resistance`, `Gargoyle Sentinel`, `Grave Bramble`, `Rambunctious Mutt`, `Secure the Scene`, `Trusty Retriever`.\n\
\n\
Opponent: 19 life.\n\
Creatures: `Liliana's Standard Bearer` (3/1), `Pit Keeper` (2/1), `Spark Reaper` (2/3 tapped).\n\
Hand: 4 cards.\n\
Graveyard: 5 cards.\n\
\n\
Strategic Assessment:\n\
`Assault Formation` is huge here. My `Carven Caryatid` is a 2/5. With Formation, it attacks as a 5/5.\n\
Also, `Assault Formation` has an activated ability: `{G}: Target creature with defender can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.`\n\
Note: `Carven Caryatid` has defender.\n\
\n\
Plan:\n\
1. Cast `Assault Formation` for {1}{G}. (Leaving {1}{W} or {G}{G} up).\n\
2. Activate `Assault Formation` for {G} to let Caryatid attack?\n\
   Cost: {1}{G} (cast) + {G} (activation) = {2}{G}{G} total? No, I have 3 Forests and 1 Plains.\n\
   Cast costs {1}{G}. Leaves 2 lands.\n\
   Activate costs {G}. Leaves 1 land.\n\
   Attacking for 5 seems good. The opponent has a 3/1 and a 2/1 untapped.\n\
   If I attack with a 5/5, they deal 3 or 2 damage back if they block? No, Formation makes creatures assign damage equal to toughness. But they still *take* damage to their toughness.\n\
   Wait, Formation says \"Each creature you control assigns combat damage equal to its toughness rather than its power.\"\n\
   So Caryatid deals 5 damage.\n\
   Opponent's blockers: 3/1, 2/1.\n\
   If they block with 3/1, they deal 3 damage to my 5 toughness Caryatid. It lives (takes 3 damage marked). Their 3/1 takes 5 damage and dies.\n\
   If they block with 2/1, same result.\n\
   If they double block? 5 power total against my 5 toughness. They would trade both for my Caryatid. That's a 2-for-1 trade in my favor.\n\
   \n\
   However, do I have enough mana?\n\
   Lands: 4 total.\n\
   Cast `Assault Formation`: {1}{G}.\n\
   Activate \"can attack\": {G}.\n\
   Total spent: {2}{G}{G}. I have 3 Forests. I can pay this.\n\
   I will have 1 mana left.\n\
   `Feat of Resistance` costs {1}{W}. I can't cast it if I spend {G}{G} total Green and {1} generic on the Formation plan unless my lands are perfect.\n\
   I have 3 Forest, 1 Plains.\n\
   Cast Formation: Use 1 Forest, 1 Plains (bad plan) or 2 Forests (fine).\n\
   If I use Forest + generic (Forest), I have Forest, Plains left.\n\
   Then activate for {G} (Forest). I have Plains left.\n\
   `Feat of Resistance` needs {1}{W}. I only have {W} left. So I can't protect it.\n\
   But `Selfless Savior` is on board! I can sac Savior to make Caryatid indestructible if they have a removal spell or a combat trick.\n\
   \n\
   Is attacking worth it?\n\
   Yes. A 5/5 beater is very strong here.\n\
\n\
Alternative:\n\
Cast `Trusty Retriever` ({3}{W}). It's a 2/3 (or 3/4 with counter).\n\
Cast `Gargoyle Sentinel` ({3}, 3/3 defender).\n\
Cast `Grave Bramble` ({1}{G}{G}, 3/4 defender). With Assault Formation next turn, this becomes a 4/4 beater.\n\
\n\
The Assault Formation line seems the most proactive and leverages my high toughness immediately. It changes the math completely.\n\
\n\
Let's go with `Assault Formation`.\n\
\n\
Steps:\n\
1. Cast `Assault Formation` (p52).\n\
2. Resolve.\n\
3. Activate it targeting `Carven Caryatid`.\n\
4. Attack with `Carven Caryatid`.\n\
5. Keep `Selfless Savior` ready.\n\
\n\
One small note: `Warmonger's Chariot` is also on the battlefield.\n\
Equip {3} adds +2/+2.\n\
If I equip Caryatid, it becomes 4/7.\n\
With Assault Formation, it deals 7 damage.\n\
But Equip costs {3}. I have 4 mana.\n\
If I equip, I can't attack (Caryatid has defender).\n\
The Chariot says: \"As long as equipped creature has defender, it can attack as though it didn't have defender.\"\n\
So if I equip Chariot ({3}), Caryatid becomes 4/7 and CAN attack.\n\
It deals 7 damage (toughness).\n\
Wait, Chariot allows attacking *without* paying the {G} to Assault Formation.\n\
And it gives +2/+2.\n\
So for {3} mana, I get a 4/7 attacker (who hits for 7).\n\
I have 4 mana. I can equip.\n\
I can attack with a 7/7 effectively.\n\
And I still have `Selfless Savior` up.\n\
\n\
Comparing options:\n\
Option A: Cast Assault Formation ({1}{G}). Activate Formation ({G}). Total {2}{G}. Caryatid is 2/5, hits for 5.\n\
Option B: Equip Warmonger's Chariot ({3}). Caryatid is 4/7. Hits for 4?\n\
   Ah, without Assault Formation, it hits for 4 (Power).\n\
   I need to cast Assault Formation AND equip?\n\
   Cast Formation ({1}{G}) + Equip ({3}) = {4}{G} = 5 mana. I have 4 lands. Can't do both.\n\
\n\
So dragging Chariot doesn't give me toughness-damage yet.\n\
If I just Equip, I have a 4/7 attacking. That's pretty good. 4 power is solid. 7 toughness is unkillable in combat here.\n\
And I save `Assault Formation` in hand for later? Or play it next turn?\n\
If I equip, I spend 3 mana. I have 1 left. `Feat of Resistance` is offline.\n\
If I cast Assault Formation and attack (paying {G}), I have a 5/5 attacking.\n\
5 damage vs 4 damage. 5 is better.\n\
Plus, `Assault Formation` is an enchantment that stays. It makes my `Selfless Savior` a 1/1 (no change).\n\
It makes `Grave Bramble` (in hand) a 4/4 later.\n\
It makes `Gargoyle Sentinel` (in hand) a 3/3 later.\n\
It makes `Carven Caryatid` a 5/5 always.\n\
\n\
The `Assault Formation` play is superior because it deals more damage (5 vs 4) and sets up the board for future defender synergies. It is permanent value.\n\
\n\
Wait, check `Warmonger's Chariot` text again. \"As long as equipped creature has defender, it can attack as though it didn't have defender.\"\n\
So equipping allows attacking.\n\
Assault Formation text: \"Target creature with defender can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.\"\n\
So I don't *need* the Chariot to attack if I have Formation and mana.\n\
\n\
Correct line: Cast Assault Formation. Activate it to let Caryatid attack.\n\
Mana used: {1}{G} + {G}. 3 mana total.\n\
Leaves 1 land up.\n\
\n\
Let's do it. Cast `Assault Formation`.\n\
\n\
One more check: `Rambunctious Mutt`. {3}{W}{W}. I have 4 lands. Can't cast. `Secure the Scene` {4}{W} cant cast.\n\
\n\
ID for Assault Formation is `p52`.\n\
\n\
Message: \"Like, look at this outfit! Toughness is the new power, darling.\"\n\
\n\
call `choose_action(choice=\"p52\")`\n\
\n\
Wait, `get_action_choices` said `Choices (7): Assault Formation...`.\n\
I will cast it.\n\
\n\
One detail: I should probably manually tap lands if `auto_tap` might screw me, but with {1}{G} cost and 3 Forests/1 Plains, auto tap will likely leave me with Forest/Plains or 2 Forests. I need {G} for the activation. So as long as it leaves a Forest, I'm good.\n\
Actually, if it leaves Plains and Forest, I can activate. If it leaves 2 Forests, I can activate.\n\
The only risk is if it uses all my green?\n\
Cost is {1}{G}. I have 3 Forests. It will use 1 Forest + 1 other. I have 1 Plains.\n\
It might use Plains + Forest. Leaving 2 Forests. Good.\n\
It might use 2 Forests. Leaving Plains + Forest. Good.\n\
It's fine.\n\
\n\
Action: Cast Assault Formation.\n\
\n\
