      "reasoning": "I literally cannot handle that Spark Reaper anymore. It's so gross.\n\
\n\
I'm blocking with three Dog tokens to kill the Spark Reaper.\n\
Attacker: `Spark Reaper` (p13).\n\
Blockers: `Dog Token` (p59), `Dog Token` (p60), `Dog Token` (p61).\n\
\n\
Block allocation:\n\
p59:p13\n\
p60:p13\n\
p61:p13\n\
\n\
This ensures lethal damage (3) on the Reaper. The Reaper has 2 power, so it will kill 2 dogs. A 2-for-1 trade, but I get rid of their engine. Plus I have plenty of dogs. Or I can just take 2 damage? I'm at 8 life. Taking 2 goes to 6. They can sac the reaper for a card and life anyway if they have mana... wait in response to blocks?\n\
They have 3 Swamps untapped? No, looking at the board:\n\
`Swamp` x6. All untapped? \"bf=[Spark Reaper 2/3 (tapped), Swamp, Swamp, Swamp, Swamp, Swamp, Swamp]\"\n\
Yes, they have plenty of mana.\n\
If I block, they can pay {3}, sac the Reaper, gain 1 life, draw a card. Then my blocks don't kill it (sacrifice removes it from combat), and I lose nothing.\n\
If I don't block, I take 2 damage. 8 -> 6.\n\
If I block with 1 dog, they might not sac it (to clear a blocker). Then I lose a dog.\n\
If I block with enough to kill it, they will almost certainly sacrifice it for value.\n\
Forcing the sacrifice is good. It removes the threat.\n\
Let's block with enough to kill it (3 dogs). Force them to use it or lose it.\n\
\n\
Playing it safe.\n\
\n\
",
