      "reasoning": "The opponent sacrificed their `Spark Reaper`. My dog tokens survived. I have 2 dogs left? Wait, checking board: `Dog Token 1/1` (token), `Dog Token 1/1` (token). Yes, 2 left. Where are the others? Ah, I blocked with 3, they sacrificed the reaper... wait, if they sacrificed it, combat damage isn't dealt, so my blockers should survive. Wait, did I block with 3? Yes. Why do I only have 2 left? Ah, wait, look at my previous turn action: `p57` was `Release the Dogs`. It made 4 tokens. I blocked with 3. If they sacrificed it, I should have 4 tokens.\n\
Check graveyard: `Release the Dogs`, `Carven Caryatid`... no tokens go to GY.\n\
Maybe they used removal? Or maybe the sacrifice happened AFTER damage? No, then they wouldn't get the draw.\n\
Maybe I'm miscounting.\n\
Wait, let's look at the previous turn recap if available. No recap provided.\n\
Let's just look at the current board state:\n\
`Dog Token 1/1 (token), Dog Token 1/1 (token)`\n\
I have 2 dogs.\n\
Opponent has NOTHING on board except lands. They have 4 cards in hand.\n\
\n\
My hand: `Cathar's Companion`, `Feat of Resistance`, `Gargoyle Sentinel`, `Grave Bramble`, `Rambunctious Mutt`, `Secure the Scene`, `Trusty Retriever`.\n\
Lands: 3 Forests, 1 Plains. (4 total).\n\
I have not played a land this turn. I have no land in hand.\n\
So I have 4 mana.\n\
\n\
Available plays:\n\
1.  **Attack with 2 dogs.** They deal 1 damage each (Assault Formation uses toughness 1). Total 2 damage. Opponent at 14 -> 12.\n\
2.  **Equip `Warmonger's Chariot`** ({3}).\n\
    -   Equip to a Dog.\n\
    -   Dog becomes 3/3 (`+2/+2`).\n\
    -   With Assault Formation, it uses toughness. Toughness goes from 1 to 3. So it deals 3 damage.\n\
    -   And I can attack with the equipped dog (3 dmg) + the other dog (1 dmg) = 4 dmg.\n\
    -   Leaves 1 mana up. I can hold `Feat of Resistance` ({1}{W}) if I had a white source untapped, but I used the Plains for `Release the Dogs`? Wait, lands untap. I have Plains open. Yes.\n\
    -   Wait, equip is sorcery speed. {3} mana. I have 4 lands. Leaving 1 land up.\n\
    -   So I can equip, attack for 4, and hold up `Feat of Resistance` to protect the equipped dog or push damage.\n\
    -   This seems very strong. It presents a real clock.\n\
3.  **Cast `Trusty Retriever`** ({3}{W}).\n\
    -   3/4 body (with counter).\n\
    -   Taps out.\n\
    -   Attacks next turn.\n\
4.  **Cast `Grave Bramble`** ({1}{G}{G}).\n\
    -   3/4 defender.\n\
    -   Good blocker, but opponent has no creatures.\n\
    -   I need to be proactive while their board is empty.\n\
5.  **Cast `Cathar's Companion`** ({2}{W}).\n\
    -   3/1 dog. Toughness 1. With Assault Formation, it deals 1 damage.\n\
    -   Terrible with my enchantment purely for stats.\n\
    -   (Unless I pump toughness).\n\
\n\
Equipping the Chariot seems like the best aggressive play.\n\
The Chariot makes the dog a 3/3.\n\
Opponent has open mana (swamps) and 4 cards. Likely removal (`Cast Down`, `Murder`, etc? It's Ravnica/Innistrad mix maybe?).\n\
If they try to kill the equipped dog, I have `Feat of Resistance` up! ({1}{W}).\n\
Wait, cost to equip is {3}. I have 4 lands. 4 - 3 = 1. `Feat` costs {1}{W}. That's 2 mana.\n\
I cannot equip AND hold up Feat.\n\
I have 4 lands.\n\
So if I equip, I am tapped out for protection (1 mana floating).\n\
Risky.\n\
\n\
Alternative: Cast `Trusty Retriever` ({3}{W}).\n\
It's a creature. If they remove it, fine.\n\
If they don't, next turn I can equip or attack.\n\
But the dog with chariot is immediate damage.\n\
Attacking with 2 1/1s is 2 damage.\n\
Attacking with 3/3 and 1/1 is 4 damage.\n\
Difference is 2 damage.\n\
\n\
What if I cast `Grave Bramble` ({3})?\n\
Leaves 1 mana. Still can't hold Feat.\n\
\n\
What if I just attack with the dogs (2 dmg) and pass with `Feat` up?\n\
That's very slow. They have 4 cards and empty board. They will play something bigger usage of mana.\n\
I should use my mana.\n\
\n\
Maybe `Trusty Retriever` is the play. It's a 3/4. That's a solid threat.\n\
Or I can cast `Gargoyle Sentinel` ({3}) and leave {W} up? No, Feat is {1}{W}.\n\
\n\
Wait, `Feat of Resistance` is {1}{W}.\n\
I have 4 lands.\n\
I can only cast a 2-drop and hold up Feat.\n\
My 2-drops? None. Hand: 3-drops and 4-drops.\n\
`Cathar's Companion` is 3 mana.\n\
`Gargoyle Sentinel` is 3 mana.\n\
`Trusty Retriever` is 4 mana.\n\
`Grave Bramble` is 3 mana.\n\
\n\
So I can't hold up protection no matter what I do, unless I do nothing.\n\
Doing nothing is bad.\n\
So I should just play the strongest threat or best value.\n\
\n\
Equipping Chariot turns a 1/1 into a 3/3. That's +2 power/toughness essentially.\n\
Casting `Trusty Retriever` adds a 3/4 body.\n\
Adding a body is generally better against spot removal (edict protection, wide board).\n\
Also `Trusty Retriever` retrieves an artifact/enchantment from GY if I choose that mode... do I have one?\n\
GY: `Carven Caryatid` (creature), `Crushing Canopy` (instant), `Release the Dogs` (sorcery), `Selfless Savior` (creature).\n\
No artifacts/enchantments in GY.\n\
So Retriever is just a 2/3 that gets a counter -> 3/4.\n\
A 3/4 is good.\n\
\n\
Effectively:\n\
Option A: Equip Chariot. Attacks for 4 total. Vulnerable to 1 removal spell leaving me with 1 creature.\n\
Option B: Cast Retriever. Attacks for 2 total (dogs). End turn with 3 creatures (two 1/1s, one 3/4).\n\
If they have a removal spell, they kill one. I still have 2.\n\
Option B is safer against 1-for-1 removal.\n\
And a 3/4 is a good stat line.\n\
\n\
Let's cast `Trusty Retriever`.\n\
When it enters, I choose \"Put a +1/+1 counter on it\". (Mode 1).\n\
I'll select `choice=\"p25\"` (Trusty Retriever).\n\
\n\
Wait, Chariot equip cost is {3}.\n\
If I equip, I attack with a 3/3 and a 1/1.\n\
If they kill the 3/3, I have a 1/1 left and the equipment.\n\
If I play Retriever, I attack with two 1/1s.\n\
Next turn I can equip the Retriever? No, Retriever is not a defender?\n\
`Warmonger's Chariot`: \"Equipped creature gets +2/+2. As long as equipped creature has defender, it can attack as though it didn't have defender.\"\n\
It gives stats to ANY creature. The defender attacking part is a bonus.\n\
So Retriever becomes 5/6 with Chariot. Nice.\n\
\n\
I think building the board wide is better than going tall on a token right now.\n\
I'll cast `Trusty Retriever`.\n\
\n\
