      "reasoning": "Attacking with the dogs again.\n\
My board: `Grave Bramble` (3/4, sick), `Wall of Vines` (0/3, sick), `Dog Token` x2 (1/1).\n\
Opponent board: `Ossuary Rats` (3/2, sick).\n\
The Rats are sick and cannot block.\n\
Wait, `Ossuary Rats` entered on their turn. It's now MY turn (Turn 10).\n\
So Rats are NOT sick anymore.\n\
Wait, turn structure:\n\
Active Player: Gem3P Valley (Me).\n\
Opponent `Ossuary Rats` is marked `(sick)` by the engine?\n\
Let's check the board state from `pass_priority`.\n\
`Ossuary Rats 3/2 (sick)`.\n\
If it says sick, it must have summoning sickness.\n\
But wait, if it was cast on their turn (Turn 9 presumably, or did they cast it on MY turn? No, it's a sorcery speed creature usually unless flash).\n\
`Ossuary Rats` does not have flash.\n\
If they cast it on THEIR turn, it would not be sick on MY turn.\n\
Why is it marked sick?\n\
Could it be `Liliana's Standard Bearer`? No, that has flash.\n\
Ah, maybe they played it on my turn via something? No.\n\
Maybe the turn counter is weird.\n\
Or maybe the \"sick\" status persists until it STARTS a turn under controller's control. Which it has not yet? (They cast it Turn 9, passed to me Turn 10).\n\
Correct, summoning sickness only wears off at the start of YOUR turn. So for THEM (non-active player), it has been under their control since the start of MY turn?\n\
Rule 302.6: A creature's activated ability with the tap symbol in its activation cost can't be activated unless the creature has been under its controller's control continuously since his or her most recent turn began.\n\
So for blocking, sickness doesn't matter. You can block with a sick creature.\n\
The \"(sick)\" label is just informational about attacking/tapping.\n\
It CAN block.\n\
\n\
Okay, so `Ossuary Rats` (3/2) can block.\n\
If I attack with 2 dogs (1/1):\n\
They block 1 dog with Rats.\n\
Rats (3/2) vs Dog (1/1, damage via toughness 1).\n\
Dog deals 1 damage to Rats -> Rats takes 1 damage (survives with 1).\n\
Rats deals 3 damage to Dog -> Dog dies.\n\
Result: I lose a dog, they take nothing (except 1 damage on the rat).\n\
Is it worth it?\n\
I have `Grave Bramble` and `Wall of Vines` holding the ground.\n\
I don't need the dogs to block. The Rats (3/2) can't get through `Grave Bramble` (3/4) or `Wall of Vines` (0/3 -> dies, but kills rats).\n\
Wait, Wall of Vines (0/3) deals 3 damage (Assault Formation). Rats (3/2). They trade.\n\
So I'm safe on blocks.\n\
Do I want to throw away a dog to deal damage to the rat?\n\
Not really. The rat is a 3/2. It dies to almost anything I have (Wall, Bramble, Sentinel, Mutt).\n\
Throwing away a dog for 1 damage on a creature that will die anyway isn't great.\n\
I'll hold the dogs back. Maybe I draw an anthem or can equip one later.\n\
Or maybe double block later?\n\
\n\
I'll pass on attacking.\n\
\n\
",
