      "reasoning": "The opponent traded `Ossuary Rats` with `Wall of Vines`.\n\
The `Malefic Scythe` now has 2 soul counters (+2/+2 effect).\n\
That's dangerous.\n\
I have a `Rambunctious Mutt` ({3}{W}{W}) in hand.\n\
It enters and destroys target artifact or enchantment an opponent controls!\n\
Target `Malefic Scythe`!\n\
This is the perfect answer.\n\
But Mutt costs {3}{W}{W}.\n\
I have 4 lands.\n\
I have a land in hand: `Thriving Heath`.\n\
I can play `Thriving Heath` (tapped).\n\
5 lands total.\n\
But Mutt costs 5 mana.\n\
Can I cast it this turn?\n\
No, the land enters tapped.\n\
So I have 4 mana available.\n\
Next turn I have 5 mana.\n\
\n\
So this turn I need to survive/setup.\n\
My lands: 3 Forests, 1 Plains.\n\
I play `Thriving Heath` (tapped). Choose a color. Say Green or Blue? Or just Green for consistency.\n\
Then I have 4 mana up.\n\
What can I do for 4 mana?\n\
- Equip `Warmonger's Chariot` ({3}).\n\
  -   Leaves {W} up.\n\
  -   Makes a creature +2/+2.\n\
  -   If I equip `Grave Bramble` (3/4), it becomes 5/6.\n\
  -   And it can attack as though it didn't have defender!\n\
  -   With Assault Formation, it uses toughness (6). Hits for 6 damage!\n\
  -   Opponent has NO creatures. Just lands and the Scythe.\n\
  -   This hits for 6. Opponent at 12 -> 6. HUGE.\n\
  -   Plus I have `Feat of Resistance` ({1}{W}).\n\
  -   Wait, equip is sorcery speed. {3} mana.\n\
  -   I have one Plains. If I tap 3 Forests for equip, I have Plains left.\n\
  -   I can hold up `Feat of Resistance`!\n\
  -   This puts lethal pressure on them. They must answer a 5/6 attacker.\n\
  -   And next turn I cast `Rambunctious Mutt` to blow up the Scythe.\n\
\n\
This is the play.\n\
1. Play land `Thriving Heath` (tapped).\n\
2. Equip `Warmonger's Chariot` to `Grave Bramble`.\n\
