`Bone Picker` is Flash-able if creature died? No, Picker is creature. It has cost reduction if creature died. It does not have Flash.\n\
So they can't flash Picker.\n\
Only `Standard Bearer` has Flash.\n\
If they flash Bearer, they have a blocker.\n\
I handle that with Feat (Pro Black) on Bramble?\n\
If I Pacify Painter, they Flash Bearer.\n\
Board: Pacified Painter, Bearer.\n\
I have Bramble, Sentinel, Dog, Dog.\n\
I attack with All (using Feat on Bramble).\n\
Bramble (Unblockable).\n\
Bearer blocks Sentinel. Sentinel dies. Bearer dies.\n\
Dogs unblocked.\n\
Damage: 5 (Bramble) + 1 + 1 = 7.\n\
Opponent at 3.\n\
Still very good.\n\
If I don't Pacify:\n\
Painter blocks Bramble. (If Bramble has Pro Black? Then Painter can't block).\n\
Wait!\n\
If I give Bramble Pro Black (`Feat of Resistance`), Painter (Black) CANNOT BLOCK IT.\n\
So Feat of Resistance makes Bramble unblockable anyway!\n\
So do I need Pacifism?\n\
If I Feat Bramble {1}{W}, Bramble is unblockable (5 damage).\n\
Painter blocks Sentinel (3 damage). Sentinel blocked.\n\
Dog (1) blocked? No, 1 blocker only.\n\
Damage: 5 + 1 + 1 = 7.\n\
Opponent at 3.\n\
Same result as flashing Bearer.\n\
But Pacifism REMOVES the blocker permanently (mostly).\n\
And if I Pacify Painter, then my Feat of Resistance is basically \"Give Bramble +1/+1\".\n\
If I didn't Pacify, Feat gives \"Unblockable +1/+1\".\n\
So Pacifism is redundant for evasion if I use Feat?\n\
Wait.\n\
If I Feat Bramble, Painter can block Sentinel.\n\
If I Pacify Painter, Painter can BLOCK NOTHING.\n\
Then Sentinel attacks UNBLOCKED.\n\
Unblocked Sentinel = 3 damage.\n\
So Pacifism adds 3 damage to the total!\n\
Case A (Feat only): 7 damage.\n\
Case B (Pacifism + Feat): 10 damage.\n\
10 damage is LETHAL.\n\
So Pacifism is CRITICAL to get Sentinel through.\n\
\n\
Confirmed. Pacifism is the play.\n\
