I will attempt to finish them off if they didn't block.\n\
Or pump if they did block but it's not shown?\n\
Logic:\n\
If I pass, damage happens (if no blocks).\n\
If I pump `Assault Formation` now:\n\
 Creatures get +0/+1.\n\
 Bramble 5/7.\n\
 Sentinel 3/4.\n\
 Dog 1/2.\n\
 Dog 1/2.\n\
 Damage increases.\n\
If I pass, damage happens.\n\
If they block, I will get priority *after* blockers are declared.\n\
So if I am seeing this screen, either:\n\
A) We are still in Declare Attackers (Opponent hasn't blocked yet).\n\
B) We are in Declare Blockers and Opponent chose NO BLOCKS.\n\
C) We are in Declare Blockers and Opponent blocked, but display issue?\n\
Given `Fetid Imp` has Deathtouch, they likely want to block.\n\
Imp (1/2 Deathtouch) can kill Bramble or Sentinel.\n\
Zombie (2/3) can block.\n\
Soldier (1/1) can block.\n\
They have 3 blockers. I have 4 attackers.\n\
They are at 2 life.\n\
Unless they block everything perfectly or kill my attackers...\n\
Wait, 3 blockers vs 4 attackers. 1 gets through.\n\
Damage will be at least 1 (Dog).\n\
Does 1 damage kill them?\n\
They are at 2 life.\n\
No, 1 damage leaves them at 1 life.\n\
I NEED `Assault Formation` pump (+0/+1) to make Dog deal 2 damage.\n\
So, regardless of blocks, I should pump to ensure lethal.\n\
BUT... if I pump now (in Attackers step), they might change blocks?\n\
No, if I pump in Attackers step, they know the math before blocking.\n\
If I wait for Blockers step, they declare blocks first. Then I pump.\n\
This is better.\n\
If we are in Attackers step, I should PASS so we get to Blockers.\n\
If we are in Blockers step (and they didn't block?), I should PUMP.\n\
How to distinguish?\n\
\"Combat: Grave Bramble -> ...\"\n\
Usually, if blockers are declared, it says: \"Grave Bramble (blocked by Imp) -> ...\"\n\
So either No Blocks, or Not Yet Blocked.\n\
If Not Yet Blocked (Attackers Step), I pass.\n\
If No Blocks (Blockers Step), I *must* pump to kill (1 unblocked dog = 1 dmg).\n\
Wait, Bramble is 5/6. Sentinel 3/3. Dog 1/1. Dog 1/1.\n\
If unblocked:\n\
Bramble deals 6? (Assault Formation: damage = toughness).\n\
Yes, Bramble toughness is 6.\n\
If *any* creature is unblocked, it deals >2 damage.\n\
Even Dog is 1/1. Toughness 1.\n\
Wait, Dog toughness is 1.\n\
So unblocked Dog deals 1.\n\
If they block Bramble, Sentinel, and one Dog...\n\
One Dog is unblocked.\n\
It deals 1 damage.\n\
Opponent goes to 1 life.\n\
So I DO need to pump.\n\
The question is WHEN.\n\
If I pump now, I spend {2}{G} (3 mana). I have 6. I can pump twice.\n\
If I pump now, they know they must block everything to survive (which they can't, they have 3 blockers).\n\
So one Dog gets through as 1/2 (2 dmg).\n\
They die.\n\
If I wait, they might make a mistake?\n\
But standard play: Wait for blocks.\n\
Only risk: If I am currently in Blockers Step with NO BLOCKS, and I pass... Combat Damage happens immediately.\n\
If Combat Damage happens with unblocked Dog (1/1), it deals 1. Opponent lives.\n\
Is it possible they declared No Blocks?\n\
Unlikely. They are at 2 life.\n\
They would *definitely* block to survive.\n\
So we must be in Declare Attackers step still?\n\
Or they blocked, and the display is just \"Combat: ...\"?\n\
Let's check `incoming_attackers` or similar in raw JSON? I don't see it.\n\
I see `game_seq 809`.\n\
I'll bet we are still in Declare Attackers because of the priority passes.\n\
(Me pass -> Op ability -> Me pass -> Op pass).\n\
So now we go to Blockers.\n\
So I will PASS.\n\
If by chance we are in Blockers and they didn't block, I might miss lethal this turn?\n\
No, if they didn't block, unblocked Bramble deals 6. Kill.\n\
Ah! Bramble is 5/6!\n\
Unblocked Sentinel is 3/3 (3 dmg). Kill.\n\
Unblocked Dog is 1/1 (1 dmg). No Kill.\n\
So if they No Block, they take 6+3+1+1 = 11. They die.\n\
So I don't need to pump if they No Block.\n\
The only scenario where I need to pump is if they block Bramble, Sentinel, and one Dog.\n\
Leaving one Dog unblocked.\n\
So I wait for blocks.\n\
