  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "MstLg Tinker passed priority during combat with Spark Reaper blocked by the 2/5 Carven Caryatid (a brick wall). They could have sacrificed Spark Reaper to its own ability (pay 3 mana) to draw a card and gain 1 life, then in postcombat main cast Bone Picker for just {B} (since a creature died this turn), netting a 3/2 flying deathtouch creature. Instead, Spark Reaper just bounces off the Caryatid accomplishing nothing.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, letting combat damage resolve with no effect (2/3 vs 2/5, both survive).",
      "better_line": "Activate Spark Reaper's ability (sacrifice itself, pay {3}) to draw a card and gain 1 life before damage. Then in postcombat main phase, cast Bone Picker for {B} (discounted since a creature died). This converts an ineffective ground creature into a 3/2 flying deathtouch + card advantage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 118,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Timed out and passed the postcombat main phase with 4 untapped Swamps and multiple strong plays available. Most critically, Barter in Blood would have forced the opponent to sacrifice both their creatures (Selfless Savior and Carven Caryatid) while only costing the Spark Reaper. This would have devastated the opponent's board, especially since the Caryatid could become a 4/7 attacker with Warmonger's Chariot. Selfless Savior's ability doesn't help against sacrifice effects.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed without casting anything, wasting 4 mana and a critical turn.",
      "better_line": "Cast Barter in Blood to force both players to sacrifice two creatures. Opponent loses Selfless Savior and Carven Caryatid; you lose only Spark Reaper (sacrificing one, then having no second creature to sacrifice). This clears the opponent's board and sets up future turns with Bone Picker (cheap after a creature dies) and Liliana's Standard Bearer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 122,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 29,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Timed out during postcombat main phase with 4 untapped Swamps and multiple strong plays available. Failed to deploy any creature, wasting an entire turn of development while behind on board.",
      "action_taken": "No response (timeout) — passed the turn with 4 mana unused and 5 castable spells in hand.",
      "better_line": "Cast Bone Picker for {3}{B} to deploy a 3/2 flying deathtouch threat, applying significant evasive pressure. Alternatively, Suspicious Shambler (4/2 with graveyard upside) or Moodmark Painter (giving Spark Reaper menace and +1/+0) would also have been strong plays.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 122,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 29,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to attack with Selfless Savior when the opponent has no untapped creatures and no untapped lands. This is 1 free damage with zero risk. Selfless Savior can still use its sacrifice ability on subsequent turns.",
      "action_taken": "Did not attack with any creatures.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Selfless Savior for 1 unblocked damage. The opponent has no blockers available and no mana for tricks.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 133,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 32,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Player timed out and assigned no blockers. Carven Caryatid (2/5) could have cleanly blocked Spark Reaper (2/3) with no risk, saving 2 damage. Additionally, Crushing Canopy could have been cast to destroy the flying Bone Picker, saving another 3 damage. Instead, the player took the full 5 damage.",
      "action_taken": "No response (timeout) — no blockers assigned, took 5 combat damage.",
      "better_line": "Block Spark Reaper with Carven Caryatid (saves 2 life, Caryatid survives). Optionally also cast Crushing Canopy targeting Bone Picker to destroy it and save 3 more life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 145,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 37,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "MstLg Tinker passed with Crushing Canopy on the stack targeting Bone Picker, missing the opportunity to sacrifice Bone Picker to Spark Reaper in response (draw a card, gain 1 life, fizzle Canopy), then after combat damage kills Spark Reaper, flash in Liliana's Standard Bearer to draw 2 more cards (2 creatures died this turn). Instead, both creatures die for no value.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, letting Crushing Canopy resolve and destroy Bone Picker with no response.",
      "better_line": "Activate Spark Reaper sacrificing Bone Picker (3 mana: draw 1, gain 1 life, fizzle Canopy). After combat damage kills Spark Reaper, flash in Liliana's Standard Bearer (2 mana) to draw 2 cards. Net result: 3 extra cards drawn and 1 life gained.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 156,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Liliana's Standard Bearer during postcombat main when no creatures died this turn, drawing 0 cards from its ETB trigger. This wastes the card's primary value (flash + card draw after a board wipe or combat deaths). The 3/1 body is fragile and provides less board presence than alternatives.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Liliana's Standard Bearer for 3 mana, getting a 3/1 body with 0 cards drawn.",
      "better_line": "Cast Suspicious Shambler (4/2 for 4 mana) for a bigger, more impactful body with graveyard recursion upside, while holding Liliana's Standard Bearer for a turn where creatures die to get actual card advantage from its ETB. Alternatively, hold up mana and pass, since the 3/1 body doesn't meaningfully change the board state.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 159,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 44,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Opponent has all lands tapped and no untapped creatures that can block. Selfless Savior could have attacked alongside Carven Caryatid for 1 additional free damage (6 total instead of 5) with zero risk.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Carven Caryatid (5 damage via Assault Formation)",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Selfless Savior and Carven Caryatid for 6 total damage, since the opponent has no untapped blockers and no mana available for instant-speed interaction.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 185,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 51,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to block Carven Caryatid which deals 5 damage (due to Assault Formation) with available blockers. Pit Keeper (2/1) is a low-value creature that already used its ETB, and blocking with it would prevent 5 damage while also putting another creature card in the graveyard to fuel Moodmark Painter and Ossuary Rats. Taking 5 damage (19→14) to preserve a 2/1 for Barter in Blood sacrifice fodder is a poor trade.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to block, taking 5 damage from the Caryatid.",
      "better_line": "Block with Pit Keeper to prevent 5 damage. Even if planning Barter in Blood next turn, having 2 creatures to sacrifice (Bearer + Reaper) while opponent loses their 2 creatures achieves the same board-clearing effect, and you save 5 life. The extra creature in graveyard also powers up Undergrowth cards.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 188,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 52,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Blocked Pit Keeper (2/1) with Selfless Savior instead of blocking Liliana's Standard Bearer (3/1). Both blocks result in trades (both creatures have 1 toughness), but blocking the Standard Bearer saves 1 more damage (3 instead of 2) and removes a more threatening creature (3/1 flash vs 2/1).",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Pit Keeper (2/1) with Selfless Savior (1/1), saving 2 damage and trading with a 2/1.",
      "better_line": "Block Liliana's Standard Bearer (3/1) with Selfless Savior (1/1), saving 3 damage and trading with a more valuable 3/1 creature.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 203,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 56,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Missed lethal damage. Opponent is at 8 life with all lands tapped and all creatures having summoning sickness (4 Dog tokens are sick). Casting Moodmark Painter (4 creature cards in graveyard = +4/+0 with menace) targeting Spark Reaper would make it a 6/3 with menace. Attacking with both Spark Reaper (6/3 menace) and Moodmark Painter (2/3) deals exactly 8 damage for the kill, with no available blockers on the opponent's side.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main phase, ending the turn without casting any spells or attacking.",
      "better_line": "Cast Moodmark Painter targeting Spark Reaper (giving it +4/+0 and menace), then attack with Spark Reaper (6/3) and Moodmark Painter (2/3) for 8 total damage — exactly lethal against the opponent at 8 life with no untapped blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 232,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 62,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The opponent has no creatures that can block (Ossuary Rats is summoning sick). Both 1/1 Dog tokens could attack for 2 free damage, bringing the opponent from 12 to 10. At 8 life, Gem3P Valley is behind on life and should be taking every opportunity to deal free damage.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to attack with either Dog token.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both 1/1 Dog tokens for 2 unblockable damage, reducing the opponent to 10 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 298,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 94,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Ossuary Rats (4/3) is blocked by Wall of Vines (0/3) which deals 3 damage via Assault Formation, killing both creatures. Village Rites could sacrifice the doomed Ossuary Rats to draw 2 cards at no real cost - the creature dies in combat regardless. All opponent lands are tapped so there's no risk of a combat trick changing the outcome.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, letting combat resolve without casting Village Rites",
      "better_line": "Cast Village Rites sacrificing Ossuary Rats to draw 2 cards for {B}, since the Rats were going to die in combat anyway - pure card advantage for essentially free.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 319,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 103,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Player timed out on Thriving Heath color choice. The auto-selected color was likely Blue (first option), which produces zero value for this WG deck. Green was the clear correct choice to supplement their green mana for Assault Formation activations ({G} and {2}{G} abilities) and potential future green spells.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out, likely auto-selecting Blue for Thriving Heath",
      "better_line": "Choose Green for Thriving Heath to have access to additional green mana for Assault Formation's activated abilities while still producing white mana for the hand full of white spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 327,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 104,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Thriving Heath color choice was made by timeout default, likely resulting in Blue being selected. The deck is WBG with no blue cards, making blue mana completely useless. Green would have been optimal to support Assault Formation's activated abilities ({G} to let defenders attack, {2}{G} for +0/+1), or Black for potential black spells in the deck.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out on Thriving Heath color choice, likely defaulting to Blue (useless color).",
      "better_line": "Choose Green to support Assault Formation's activated abilities, or Black if there are black cards in the deck.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 327,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 104,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "With Assault Formation on the battlefield (creatures deal damage equal to toughness), activating its {2}{G} ability to give all creatures +0/+1 would have made both attacking Dog tokens deal 2 damage each (4 total) instead of 1 each (2 total). The opponent is at 10 life, so doubling the combat damage is very significant. The player had exactly enough untapped mana (3 Forests + Plains) to activate this.",
