    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "With Assault Formation on the battlefield (creatures deal damage equal to toughness) and 1 untapped Forest, Gem3P Valley could activate Assault Formation's {G} ability to let Grave Bramble (3/4 defender) attack this turn, dealing 4 damage to the opponent at 10 life. The opponent's only creature (Moodmark Painter) is summoning sick and can't block. This is 4 free damage that brings the opponent to 6 life.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Assault Formation, missing the attack with Grave Bramble.",
      "better_line": "Activate Assault Formation targeting Grave Bramble for {G}, then attack with Grave Bramble for 4 damage, putting the opponent to 6 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 356,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 118,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Player timed out during precombat main phase with 5 mana available, multiple castable spells (Pacifism, Cathar's Companion, Feat of Resistance), and a strong Assault Formation board that could pressure the opponent at 10 life. Moodmark Painter is extremely dangerous with 10 creatures in opponent's graveyard (potential +10/+0 and menace). Missing the entire turn's actions at 8 life in a close game is devastating.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out - no action taken, effectively passing the entire turn.",
      "better_line": "Cast Pacifism on Moodmark Painter to neutralize its massive Undergrowth threat, then cast Cathar's Companion as an additional body. Use Assault Formation to enable Grave Bramble to attack, pressuring opponent's 10 life total.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 361,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 121,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Opponent has no untapped creatures that can block (Moodmark Painter is summoning sick). Both Dog Tokens could attack for 2 free damage with zero risk. Additionally, Gargoyle Sentinel could be activated for 3 mana to attack for 3 more (5 total damage, bringing opponent from 10 to 5). Missing 2-5 free damage against an opponent at 10 life while you're at 8 life is a significant mistake in a race situation.",
      "action_taken": "Passed combat without declaring any attackers, dealing 0 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Dog Tokens for 2 guaranteed damage. Ideally also activate Gargoyle Sentinel (3 mana) to attack for 3 flying damage, dealing 5 total and putting opponent to 5 life. Keep remaining mana open for Feat of Resistance or Assault Formation pump if needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 363,
      "player": "Gem3P Valley",
      "decision_index": 123,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Opponent is casting Pacifism on Moodmark Painter, which will render it useless. Village Rites could sacrifice the Painter in response, fizzling Pacifism and drawing 2 cards. This also increases graveyard creature count to 11, powering up the Revenant in hand.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, allowing Pacifism to resolve on Moodmark Painter",
      "better_line": "Cast Village Rites sacrificing Moodmark Painter in response to Pacifism. This fizzles Pacifism (wasting opponent's card and mana), draws 2 cards, and grows the graveyard for Revenant.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 370,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 126,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "MstLg Tinker has a Thriving Moor in hand and 1 land drop remaining in their postcombat main phase, but passes priority without playing it. This wastes a free land drop that would give them an additional mana source next turn. With cards like Caged Zombie (3 mana) and Suspicious Shambler (4 mana) in hand, plus the potential to activate Malefic Scythe's equip cost, having an extra land in play is meaningful. There's no reason not to play a tapped land in the postcombat main phase.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing Thriving Moor, ending the turn with an unused land drop.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Moor (choosing an appropriate color) to have 8 mana sources available next turn, enabling more flexibility to cast multiple spells or activate abilities.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 403,
      "player": "MstLg Tinker",
      "decision_index": 134,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Blocked a 1/1 Dog Token instead of the 5/6 Grave Bramble (dealing 6 damage via Assault Formation). Blocking the Dog prevents only 1 damage, while blocking Grave Bramble prevents 6 damage (no trample). This results in taking 7 damage (down to 3 life) instead of 2 damage (down to 8 life), putting MstLg Tinker in a critically dangerous position.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked a 1/1 Dog Token with the Soldier Token, preventing only 1 damage.",
      "better_line": "Block Grave Bramble with the Soldier Token to prevent 6 damage, going to 8 life instead of 3 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
